<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Which Game Modes this app supports, and what it refuses.

  It is not a game. The category above it in the manifest is there for the power
  path, and this file is the part that decides what the platform is allowed to do
  with that category — which for a compute app is mostly "nothing".

  `supportsBatteryGameMode` is deliberately **absent**, and that is the load-
  bearing line in this file. A mode not declared here is a mode the Game
  Dashboard does not offer, and Battery mode exists to cut clocks. Offering it on
  an app whose whole job is sustained CPU inference would hand the user a switch
  labelled "make generation slower", and an OEM that defaults games to Battery
  would flip it for them. The category is being taken *for* the clocks; declaring
  the mode that gives them back would undo the reason for the change.

  `allowGameDownscaling="false"`. The platform's downscale works by resizing the
  app's own surface. This app's surface is a Compose UI — chat text, a token
  inspector, a resource graph. Shrinking it blurs the text and saves nothing at
  all, because the cost of a run is ggml on the CPU and not the pixels drawn over
  it. The rendering was never the expensive part.

  `allowGameFpsOverride="false"`, for the same reason and a sharper one: an FPS
  cap applied to a UI that is streaming tokens makes the stream stutter while
  leaving the decode exactly as expensive as it was. It would cost the one thing
  the user can see and save the one thing they cannot.

  What is left is the half worth having: with the category set, Performance mode
  reaches `motorola.hardware.power.IMdpfExt` and Qualcomm's `IPowerModule`, which
  is what was measured on this phone holding cores at 1713-1977 MHz against a
  3321/3801 ceiling with nothing telling the platform the workload mattered.

  Unmeasured for this app. No before/after generation exists yet.
-->
<game-mode-config
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:supportsPerformanceGameMode="true"
    android:allowGameDownscaling="false"
    android:allowGameFpsOverride="false" />
